{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed first-floor element of the development\r\nwould create an unacceptable sense of enclosure, be&amp;nbsp; overbearing\r\nand an incongruous form of development that would likely impact upon daylight/sunlight, to the detriment of outlook to the residential flats at the north of the site, by virtue of\r\nits proximity&amp;nbsp; head on relationship and their respective orientations, with\r\nparticular reference to effects on the rear windows serving 7a Village Way\r\nEast. This would be contrary to Policy DM1 of Harrow’s Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan document (2013) and the relevant provisions of the adopted\r\nHarrow Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010) and\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2023&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;In the absence of justifying information, t&lt;span style=&quot;background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;&quot;&gt;he residential element of the development,\r\nby virtue of the site background noise, disturbance, poor outlook and security\r\nconcerns associated with its location within a backland parking and servicing\r\narea and issues integral to the scheme’s design, would result in a substandard form\r\nof accommodation for future occupiers of the site to the detriment of their\r\nliving conditions. The development is thereby contrary to the high quality\r\ndesign aspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policies\r\nD3, D11, D13, and D14 of The London Plan (2021), Policies DM1 and DM2 of the\r\nHarrow Development Management Policies Local Plan (2013) and the adopted\r\nSupplementary Planning Documents Residential Design Guide (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
